# Template for .prod.env (copy to platform-py/.prod.env; the real file is gitignored, chmod 600).
# Secrets: generate A NEW VALUE per server (openssl rand -hex 24). Never commit the real file.
# Usage: docker compose --env-file .prod.env -f docker-compose.yml -f docker-compose.apps.yml -f docker-compose.prod.yml up -d

# --- Public address (required) -----------------------------------------------------------
# HTTPS origin as seen by the browser (tunnel/TLS proxy). Enables Secure cookies, the OAuth/MCP issuer and links.
HUB_PUBLIC_URL=https://hub.exemplo.com.br
# Developer docs (/developers, /dev/docs/*.md) public without login (1, default); 0 = login required.
HUB_PUBLIC_DOCS=1
HUB_COOKIE_SECURE=1

# --- Infrastructure passwords (required; compose internal network) ---------------------------
# To change after the first start: ALTER USER hub on both Postgres instances and recreate app-hub-objstore; at boot the hub
# replaces the dev password (hubpy-*) inside the vault variables (app DSNs/keys) with the one here (docs F19).
APP_HUB_DB_PASSWORD=<openssl rand -hex 24>          # hub Postgres (app-hub-db)
APP_HUB_APP_DB_PASSWORD=<openssl rand -hex 24>      # apps Postgres (app-hub-app-db)
APP_HUB_OBJSTORE_PASSWORD=<openssl rand -hex 24>    # MinIO (app-hub-objstore)

# --- Internal hub -> app tokens (one per app; required) -------------------------------------
HUB_INTERNAL_TOKEN_ATIVOS=<openssl rand -hex 24>
HUB_INTERNAL_TOKEN_FORNECEDORES=<openssl rand -hex 24>
HUB_INTERNAL_TOKEN_SERVICOS=<openssl rand -hex 24>
HUB_INTERNAL_TOKEN_COLETOR=<openssl rand -hex 24>

# --- Vault -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Default: /data/master.key (volume app-hub-data, created on first boot; BACK IT UP SEPARATELY —
# without it the encrypted secrets cannot be opened). To keep it outside the volume, mount the file and point here.
# HUB_MASTER_KEY_FILE=/run/secrets/hub-master.key

# --- Network / access control ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Control plane (/api, /admin) restricted by CIDR; empty = no restriction. Behind a tunnel/proxy,
# list the trusted proxies so the client's real IP is used.
# HUB_ADMIN_ALLOWED_CIDRS=10.0.0.0/8,192.168.0.0/16
# HUB_TRUSTED_PROXIES=172.16.0.0/12
# HUB_TRUST_PROXY_HEADERS=1
# The edge (app-hub-edge, on HUB_PORT) is already trusted on its own (HUB_EDGE_CIDR = <HUB_SUBNET>.250.0/24).
# New-version notice in Administração › Saúde (one check per day against GitHub releases; nothing updates on its own):
# HUB_UPDATE_CHECK=1
# HUB_UPDATE_REPO=alvesmaia/application-hub
# Storage broker: CIDR of each app's network (already set in compose; change only if you change the networks).
# HUB_BROKER_APP_CIDRS=ativos=10.231.1.0/24,fornecedores=10.231.2.0/24,servicos=10.231.3.0/24,coletor=10.231.5.0/24
# Key that signs the identity sent to the apps (>= 32 characters); empty = random per process.
# HUB_USER_SIG_KEY=<openssl rand -hex 32>

# --- Audit and build ------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Folder OUTSIDE the data volume (another disk/NFS) that receives the audit's signed head (required).
HUB_AUDIT_HEAD_DIR=/srv/app-hub-audit-head
# Audit anchor also via webhook (POST JSON of the signed head on each event):
# HUB_AUDIT_HEAD_URL=https://ancora.empresa.com.br/hub-head
# HUB_AUDIT_HEAD_TOKEN=...   # optional: sent as Authorization: Bearer
# HUB_BUILD_CPUS=2 · HUB_BUILD_TIMEOUT_S=900 · HUB_BUILD_MEMORY=1Gi · HUB_KEEP_IMAGES=3 (rollback pinned per app/environment)

# --- Observability ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# HUB_TELEMETRY=0                     # disables metrics/traces (default: on)
# OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT=http://collector:4318

# --- Sign-in with Microsoft Entra ID (optional; see docs/IMPLANTACAO.md "Registrar o app no Entra ID") ----
# Without the first four, the "Entrar com Microsoft" button does not appear and local login stays as is.
# Redirect URI to register: <HUB_PUBLIC_URL>/auth/entra/callback
# HUB_SSO_PROVIDER=entra
# HUB_ENTRA_TENANT_ID=<tenant id>   # or organizations / common (multi-tenant)
# HUB_ENTRA_CLIENT_ID=<application (client) id>
# Client secret: in the vault (python -m hub.admin set-entra-secret, docs/IMPLANTACAO.md) or:
# HUB_ENTRA_CLIENT_SECRET_FILE=/run/secrets/entra-client-secret   # or HUB_ENTRA_CLIENT_SECRET=...
# HUB_ENTRA_ALLOWED_TENANTS=<tid1>,<tid2>   # effectively required with organizations/common
# HUB_ENTRA_ALLOWED_DOMAINS=empresa.com.br
# HUB_ENTRA_ROLE_MAP={"<objectId of the group or app role value>":"Administrador"}   # or id=Função,id2=Função
# HUB_ENTRA_DEFAULT_ROLE=Colaborador      # role for first-time sign-ins with no mapped group
# HUB_LOCAL_LOGIN=1                       # 1 = email/password for everyone · admins = administrators only · 0 = off

# --- Off-site copy of each backup (optional) -----------------------------------------------------
# The backup stays on the local object store; this sends a second copy elsewhere, reads it back and checks the sha256.
# A failure keeps the local backup and raises an alert.
# HUB_BACKUP_OFFSITE_URL=https://key:secret@s3.example.com:9000/bucket/prefix   # any S3 (another MinIO, AWS S3…)
# HUB_BACKUP_OFFSITE_URL=sharepoint://<connection>/Backups/hub   # a SharePoint connection from Administration ›
#   Connections (credentials stay in the vault). With Sites.Selected the site grant must have the "write" role.

# --- Sample apps and instance (optional; scripts/install.sh fills them in) ----------------------
# COMPOSE_PROFILES=demo-apps          # starts the 4 sample apps; without it: HUB_APPS_JSON=./apps.empty.json
# HUB_PROJECT=app-hub · HUB_PORT=8090 · HUB_BIND=127.0.0.1 · HUB_SUBNET=10.231 (several instances on the same host)
# HUB_BIND6=[::1] (= HUB_BIND outside loopback) · rootless Podman: HUB_CONTAINER_SOCKET_HOST=/run/user/<uid>/podman/podman.sock

# --- DO NOT set in production ---------------------------------------------------------------
# HUB_DEMO_USERS / HUB_DEMO_PASSWORD (demo accounts) and HUB_DEMO_E2E_HOSTILE (test routes).
# The first administrator is created with: docker compose ... run --rm --no-deps app-hub-web \
#   python -m hub.admin create-admin --email voce@empresa.com --out /data/primeiro-acesso.txt
